# Deadwind Pass - Recipes companion (pack butler-routes-completionist, v1).
# Only recipes whose SOURCE is physically in Deadwind Pass, verified against
# the local Forever game data (questie-forever item drop tables). Two ship,
# both as drop collects off sole in-zone sources: a Deadwind Warlock carries
# the Enchanting formula, and a fixed recipe object above the northern road
# holds the Cooking recipe. Nothing is sold by any in-zone vendor, and every
# other in-zone-dropping recipe is a generic multi-zone world drop; quest
# records carry no reward data (see docs/companion-unverified.md).
# Trainer-taught staples are excluded: Polestar's own profession guides cover
# those. Each step is gated to its profession; other characters skip it
# cleanly. Every other profession has no Deadwind Pass source, so that is
# stated, not padded.
guide butler-routes-completionist/deadwind-pass-recipes
title Deadwind Pass - Recipes
levels 60-60
zone Deadwind Pass
faction Alliance
category Professions
folder Companions
keywords deadwind pass, recipes, patterns, professions, companions
coords live
version 1

step Enchanting — Superior Strength bracer formula (drop)

  zone map 1430

  when skill Enchanting 1

  goto 60.51,61.69
  collect 16246 "Formula: Enchant Bracer - Superior Strength" optional
  note A Deadwind Warlock ranging the broken road is the sole dropper anywhere in the data, at about one in a hundred kills. No quest takes the formula in the data.

step Cooking — Plated Armorfish recipe (drop)

  zone map 1430

  when skill Cooking 1

  goto 52.4,34.5
  collect 286153 "Recipe: Plated Armorfish" optional
  note The fixed recipe object above the northern road is the sole source anywhere in the data; the drop rate is not in the data. No quest takes the recipe in the data.

step Blacksmithing, Alchemy, Tailoring and the rest — no Deadwind Pass source
  note No Blacksmithing plan, Alchemy recipe, Tailoring pattern, Engineering schematic, Fishing lure, or First Aid manual has a source physically in Deadwind Pass in the data; trainer-taught staples live in Polestar's own profession guides.
